<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Jannaeus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 76 BCE</span> · Also known as Alexander Yannai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Jannaeus was king and high priest of the Hasmonean kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judaea</a> from 103 to 76 BCE. Through constant wars he extended the kingdom to its greatest size, taking coastal cities and lands east of the Jordan. His harsh suppression of a Pharisee-led revolt made his reign one of internal strife.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-jannaeus.jpg" alt="Alexander Jannaeus" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Reverdy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_Jannaeus_medal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
